		"meta": {
			"author": "",
			"category": null,
			"deploymentTarget": {
				"branch": "master",
				"name": "Wire",
				"version": {
					"major": 7,
					"minor": 20,
					"patch": 0
				}
			},
			"description": "The first in a series of tutorials on collections. Here you will learn about what collections are and how to instantiate nodes.",
			"displayName": "Collection Fundamentals",
			"identifier": "a09b1110-c398-4ea9-bb07-2382c0690b4f",
			"licenseName": "",
			"mail": "",
			"originalTarget": {
				"branch": "master",
				"name": "Wire",
				"version": {
					"major": 7,
					"minor": 18,
					"patch": 0
				}
			},
			"quality": 32856,
			"resolution": {
				"height": 1080,
				"width": 1920
			},
			"saveTarget": {
				"branch": "7.20.0",
				"name": "Wire",
				"version": {
					"major": 7,
					"minor": 20,
					"patch": 0
				}
			},
			"thumbnail": "",
			"url": "",
			"vendor": ""
		},
		"nextNodeId": 32,
		"nodes": {
			"0": {
				"attributes": {
					"alignment": {
						"type": "integer",
						"value": 0
					},
					"fill": {
						"type": "bool",
						"value": true
					},
					"font-size": {
						"type": "float",
						"value": 19
					},
					"text": {
						"type": "string",
						"value": "COLLECTIONS\n\nThus far we've been demonstrating everything with single nodes. A single Circle here and a single texture there. \nBut it is easy to imagine visuals with hundreds of shapes and images at the same time.\n\nWe do not want you to make hundreds of nodes to achieve that. \nFor this problem we'd like to introduce you to the concept of instances and collections.\nWe will explore most of this in the basic and advanced tutorials, but for now it is important that you understand the concept.\n\nNearly every node in Wire can be instantiated.\nThis means that multiple instances of that particular node live inside that node.\nIn practical terms, instead of making 100 Circle nodes, you make a single circle node and instantiate it a hundred times.\nA signal that carries multiple instances of a node is referred to as a collection.\n\nWe don't expect that you fully understand how instancing works after this tutorial.\nThis tutorial is only meant to introduce the general concept and its existence.\nIn the basic course we will use examples that use instancing, so it is good to already know a bit of what lies ahead in the future."
					}
				},
				"bounds": {
					"height": 357.581756591796875,
					"width": 911,
					"x": 207,
					"y": 212.276336669921875
				},
				"class": {
					"id": "77697265-3C1D-467D-A722-0FC566538374",
					"version": 1
				},
				"clock": "video",
				"color": "ffd0c117",
				"constants": {},
				"hidden": [
					"text",
					"alignment",
					"font-size",
					"fill"
				],
				"name": "Comment",
				"thumbnail_visible": true
			},
			"1": {
				"attributes": {
					"alignment": {
						"type": "integer",
						"value": 0
					},
					"fill": {
						"type": "bool",
						"value": false
					},
					"font-size": {
						"type": "float",
						"value": 19
					},
					"text": {
						"type": "string",
						"value": "INSTANTIATED NODES\n\nThe Float node below has 5 instances.\nBy selecting the node and looking at the number left of the main outlet you can find how many instances there are.\nThis value can also be found  (and adjusted) in the node panel.\n\nWhen hovering over the outlet of the node, a list of values will appear.\nThese are the values of each instance of the node, under the attribute section.\n\nThe value box displays \"multiple\".\nThis means that there are multiple instances of this node with different values.\n\nTo edit the values, hold the CMD\/CTRL key while clicking on the value box.\nAlternatively, you can edit the input values by clicking on the list icon in the node panel (right of the +\/- symbols).\n\nAssignment: create a Color node, set it to 5 instances in the node panel and give each instance a different color."
					}
				},
				"bounds": {
					"height": 501.21063232421875,
					"width": 911.54718017578125,
					"x": 207,
					"y": 597
				},
				"class": {
					"id": "77697265-3C1D-467D-A722-0FC566538374",
					"version": 1
				},
				"clock": "video",
				"color": "ffff6a00",
				"constants": {},
